hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18051","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Ibn Tawus from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in al-Najm, and the people prostrated with him. Al-Muttalib said: And I did not prostrate with them, and he was at that time a polytheist. Al-Muttalib said: Then I shall never leave prostration in it ever."
"18052","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us from Mamar from Ibn Tawus from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Jafar ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Makkah Surah al-Najm, then he prostrated, and whoever was with him prostrated, then I raised my head and refused to prostrate, and al-Muttalib had not become Muslim that day, and after that he would not hear anyone reciting it except he prostrated with him."
